# 🔌 Electronic Design, Component Justifications & Circuit Architecture

This document provides a comprehensive analysis of the electronic hardware selection, power distribution hierarchy, master pinout netlist, and mandatory safety interlocks for the **Robo Grand Prix** autonomous race car.

---

Electronic Hardware Details & Engineering Justifications

| Component | Selected Part & Specifications | Power Rail | Engineering Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Microcontroller (MCU)** | **ESP32-WROOM-32U**<br>• Dual-Core 32-bit @ 240 MHz<br>• 520 KB SRAM<br>• Native PWM & Dual UART | `5.0V DC` (via Buck) | Dual-core architecture isolates high-speed sensor polling (Core 0 at 250 Hz) from PID steering and speed calculations (Core 1). The 32U variant features an external IPEX antenna port to prevent electromagnetic interference (EMI) from the adjacent motor. |

| **Front Obstacle Sensor** | **TF-Luna Micro LiDAR**<br>• Time-of-Flight (ToF) Infrared<br>• Range: 0.2m – 8.0m<br>• UART @ 115,200 baud | `5.0V DC` (via Buck) | Ultrasonic sensors suffer from echo delays at high speeds. ToF LiDAR scans up to 8 meters ahead at 250 Hz, giving the system adequate distance lead-time for high-speed trajectory planning. |

| **Side Wall Sensors** | **Sharp GP2Y0A21YK0F (x2)**<br>• Analog IR Distance Sensors<br>• Range: 10cm – 80cm<br>• Response Time: 38.3ms | `5.0V DC` (via Buck) | Outputs an analog voltage read directly via ESP32 ADC pins (`GPIO 34` & `35`), avoiding I2C/UART bus contention while providing continuous short-range feedback to keep the car centered. |

| **Steering Actuator** | **DS3218MG Servo**<br>• 20 kg·cm Torque @ 6.0V<br>• Full CNC Metal Gears<br>• Speed: 0.14 sec/60° | `5.0V DC` (via Buck) | Standard plastic-gear servos strip under high-speed cornering loads or wall impacts. The 20 kg·cm metal gear train maintains reliable Ackerman steering control under extreme lateral acceleration. |

| **Main Motor Drive** | **60A Sensorless Brushless ESC**<br>• Continuous Current: 60A<br>• Burst Current: 320A<br>• Input: 2S–3S LiPo | `7.4V DC` (Direct LiPo) | The vehicle draws ~10A on average and 30A during peak acceleration. A 60A rated ESC operates well below its thermal limits, preventing thermal throttling or power shutoffs. |

| **Voltage Regulator** | **DC-DC Step-Down Buck Converter**<br>• Input: 7.4V – 12V<br>• Output: 5.0V @ 3.0A Continuous | In: `7.4V`<br>Out: `5.0V` | Isolates sensitive 5V logic electronics from main motor voltage sag. Operates at >90% switching efficiency compared to inefficient linear regulators. |

| **Primary Power Source** | **2S LiPo Battery Pack**<br>• Nominal Voltage: 7.4V<br>• High C-Rating Discharge | `7.4V DC` Nominal | Provides high current output with minimal internal resistance to drive the propulsion motor and power bus simultaneously. |

